WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.300
Parents visiting their child's school
are frequently greeted with a raft of

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.740
impressive-sounding but impenetrable
education jargon.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:17.000
One result: even informed parents
can walk away frustrated

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.480
and unsure if their child is in good hands.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:26.120
So, here are five questions to ask – before the first day of school this year – that can help cut through the noise.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:30.620
One: what's the best thing my child
is going to read this year?

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.860
Two: what one or two values are at
the heart of our school's culture,

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.280
and how will they be applied?

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.100
Three: in the typical month, how many hours
will be devoted to tests and test preparation?

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:50.080
Four: what's the one paper or project that I should
expect my child to come home excited about?

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.720
Five: what's the most important thing that
you think I can do to help my child

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:01.100
be academically successful this year? These questions are hard to spin and resistant to jargon.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:07.800
And, no matter the answer, you'll walk
away with real insight into the year ahead.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.060
What do you think makes for a good
classroom? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.369
Also, let us know what other topics you'd
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:25.100
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for
more research and videos from AEI.

